1. The Core InfrastructureStandard Libraries#include <stdio.h>: Handles standard input and output functions (like printf and scanf).#include <math.h>: The heart of the calculator. This library provides advanced mathematical functions such as pow(), sqrt(), sin(), log10(), and log().#include <stdlib.h>: Used here for standard system utilities.Constant Definitions#define PI 3.14159265358979323846: C does not have a native, universally standardized value for $\pi$ built into every compiler environment. Defining this precisely is critical for accurate trigonometric conversions.2. The Architecture & Flow ControlThe program relies on an infinite event loop (while (1)) to keep the calculator running continuously. This mimics a real physical calculator, ensuring it doesn't shut down after processing a single calculation.       [ Start Program ]
